<title>USA: Synovus Financial Corp Q4 shr rises.</title>
<headline>Synovus Financial Corp Q4 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ga. 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.36		    $0.29</p>
<p> Net			 41,661		   33,634</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 116,332		  115,823</p>
<p>		 Year</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.20		    $1.00</p>
<p> Net			139,604		  114,583</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 116,133		  114,954</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - 1996 results include an after-tax charge of $2.8 million, or $0.024 per share, to recapitalize the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Q4 net interest income was $97.4 million vs $88.3 million.</p>
<p>Q4 provision for loan losses was $9.1 million vs $8.6 million.</p>
<p>Total assets at December 31 $8.6 billion vs $7.9 billion. Net loans at December 31 $5.97 billion vs $5.43 billion. Total deposits at December 31 $7.2 billion vs $6.7 billion.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
